>That is my understanding of it. 

Negative AC counts as a random number between -1 and the actual AC for the
purpose of evading attacks, and also absorbs a second such random number's
worth of damage from attacks that hit.

There's probably an off-by-one error in this, and I don't care.

Monster ACs work as straight evasion, and are stupidly bad in the middle
and late game - and the player can accumulate equally absurd to-hit
bonuses, which is why you never miss.
